      "page_level_design_instruction": "**RevvLot Home Page \u2014 Full Visual Design Direction**\n\n**SIGNATURE MOMENT:** The hero section features a full-bleed, edge-to-edge marquee strip of the site name \"REVVLOT\" rendered in Arial Black at ~120px, alternating between AOL Hot Magenta and Netscape Lime, stacked in two rows and scrolling horizontally like a 90s ticker tape \u2014 it crashes through the top of the page before the navigation even settles, acting as a typographic wallpaper backdrop behind the hero content. This is unmistakably GeoCities-era maximalism: the type IS the hero image, and the pixel-art car lot illustration floats on top of it rather than beside it. This move is inevitable for the retro_90s_web aesthetic \u2014 type-as-wallpaper, neon-on-dark, zero restraint.\n\n**SECTION SEQUENCE AND RHYTHM:**\n1. Hero \u2014 Maximum density, dark portal surface (Midnight Lot), marquee type backdrop, asymmetric layout with illustration dominating the right two-thirds while CTA stack anchors bottom-left. Electric, chaotic energy.\n2. Stats \u2014 A full-bleed GeoCities Grape panel. Oversized numerals as display type \u2014 not cards, but a raw four-column data dashboard with stat values at 72\u201380px Arial Black in Netscape Lime. Sparse, punchy. Serves as a breathing beat after the hero chaos.\n3. Feature Grid \u2014 Returns to density. Bevel White raised-panel cards on a Midnight Lot background, with Browser Chrome Gray inset borders. A tiled diagonal wallpaper texture behind the grid. Retro icon anchors each card. Asymmetric: 2\u00d72 grid left-heavy with a side-column CTA strip on the right.\n4. Timeline \u2014 Masthead-style horizontal strip layout. Each step is a numbered block separated by rainbow rule dividers. Background alternates between GeoCities Grape and Midnight Lot in a hard-cut stripe per step \u2014 no gradients. Step numbers are oversized VT323 digits (80px) used as structural glyphs, not body text.\n5. Testimonials \u2014 Dense, multi-column \"guestbook\" aesthetic. Three quote blocks styled as browser window chrome panels (beveled borders, fake title bar in Browser Chrome Gray). Sunshine Honk star ratings. AOL Hot Magenta quote marks at 96px. Asymmetric alignment with quotes offset from each other vertically.\n\n**COLOR AND SURFACE USAGE:**\n- Hero: Midnight Lot background, Netscape Lime + AOL Hot Magenta for marquee type, Bevel White for subheadline prose, Sunshine Honk for eyebrow label.\n- Stats: GeoCities Grape full-bleed, Netscape Lime for numerals, Bevel White for descriptors, Dial-Up Sky underline rule beneath headline.\n- Feature Grid: Midnight Lot page background, Bevel White raised card faces, Browser Chrome Gray card borders and inset shadows, Netscape Lime for icon accent strokes, Sunshine Honk for eyebrow, AOL Hot Magenta for section headline.\n- Timeline: Alternating GeoCities Grape / Midnight Lot hard stripes, Sunshine Honk step eyebrows, Netscape Lime step titles, Bevel White body text, rainbow rule dividers between steps.\n- Testimonials: Midnight Lot background, Bevel White browser-chrome card surfaces, Browser Chrome Gray title bar strips, AOL Hot Magenta oversized quote marks, Sunshine Honk star ratings, Dial-Up Sky reviewer names as underlined links.\n\n**TYPOGRAPHIC HIERARCHY:**\n- Display / H1: Arial Black, ALL-CAPS, 56\u201372px, tight tracking (-0.02em), hard text-shadow in contrasting color. Used in hero headline and stats numerals.\n- H2 section headlines: Arial Black, ALL-CAPS, 36\u201348px, alternating between AOL Hot Magenta and Netscape Lime depending on surface.\n- H3 card/step titles: Arial Black, ALL-CAPS, 22\u201328px, Bevel White or Netscape Lime.\n- Body: Verdana, 14\u201316px, 1.65 line-height, Bevel White or near-white on dark surfaces.\n- Accent/metadata: VT323, 12\u201314px, Sunshine Honk or Dial-Up Sky \u2014 hit counters, step numbers as structural glyphs, badge labels.\n- Eyebrow labels: Verdana, ALL-CAPS, 11px, letter-spacing 0.2em, Sunshine Honk background chip with Midnight Lot text.\n\n**DENSITY / WHITESPACE LOGIC:**\nHero and testimonials are high-density with layered elements. Stats is intentionally sparse \u2014 four numbers on a flat grape field, maximum breathing room. Feature grid returns to medium-high density with tight card gutters. Timeline is structured and rhythmic, not dense. The page breathes in a dense \u2192 sparse \u2192 dense \u2192 rhythmic \u2192 dense pattern to prevent visual fatigue while maintaining 90s maximalist energy throughout.\n\n**RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR:**\n- Hero: Marquee type scales down to 60px on tablet, 36px on mobile. Illustration drops behind text on mobile (background position). CTA stack goes full-width.\n- Stats: 4-column \u2192 2-column \u2192 1-column stacked. Numerals scale from 72px \u2192 48px \u2192 40px.\n- Feature Grid: 2\u00d72 grid \u2192 2-column \u2192 1-column. Side CTA strip moves below grid on tablet/mobile.\n- Timeline: Horizontal strip \u2192 vertical stacked steps on mobile. Rainbow dividers become horizontal rules.\n- Testimonials: 3-column \u2192 1-column stacked. Quote panels maintain full browser-chrome treatment at all sizes.\n\n**FIT WITH SHARED DESIGN SYSTEM:**\nAll color tokens drawn strictly from the 8-color palette. Typography uses only Arial Black (heading), Verdana (body), and VT323 (accent) as specified. The beveled button treatment, rainbow rule dividers, 88\u00d731 badge motifs, and hit-counter widget in VT323 appear across the page as recurring structural devices, not decorative afterthoughts. The page establishes the visual language that Browse Inventory and Vehicle Specs will inherit.",
